==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|over|sell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/oʊ.vɚ.sɛl/|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-oversell.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛl|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|oversells|overselling|oversold}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[agree]] to [[sell]] more of something than one can [[supply]].
#: {{cot|en|overcommit|overpromise}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To be too [[eager]] in [[attempting]] to sell something.
#: {{ant|en|undersell}}
#: {{hypo|en|sell past the close}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[praise]] something to [[excess]].
#: {{ant|en|undersell}}
#: {{collocation|en|I don't want to '''oversell''' it, but [second clause]}}
#: {{ux|en|I don't want to '''oversell''' it, but you've got to check out that new restaurant on Third Street.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To sell for a higher price than; to exceed in sale price.
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|The Chances|passage=One whose beauty / Would '''oversell''' all Italy}}

